+# Zentral Extended 3.0.0 — install and test
+
+Original Zentral reference: **1.1.0**, pinned in `UPSTREAM.json`.
+
+## Install this package
+
+1. Export your current Extended settings and keep a copy of the old mod folder.
+2. Close Zen completely, replace the old Extended folder with this archive's `zentral/` folder, then start Zen. Keep the folder name used by your existing Sine registration; Core resolves its own root.
+3. The package's `theme.json` registers only `loader/Zentral.uc.js`. If Sine has cached old script registrations, refresh/re-enable the mod so it reads that metadata. Never enable the separate original Zentral at the same time.
+4. Open Extended Settings (Ctrl+Alt+=) and verify the version is 3.0.0. Existing profile choices are preserved. New choices appear under Panel layout, Navigation toolbar, Simple appearance, Detailed appearance → Floating pill, Shortcuts, Video playback and Compatibility.
+
+## First testing pass
+
+- Open a normal app. Use Detach in the pill, then Move. Drag near an edge for a docking preview. Confirm closing/reopening and restarting restores the app's placement.
+- Try different apps and use RMB → Reset position on an app tile or the panel's toolbar/pill. With the global placement scope, reset affects the shared placement.
+- Allow partial overflow under Panel layout. Move a detached panel near all edges and verify the pill is reachable. Hover reveal remains its own setting and still uses the panel's remembered dock side as its edge target.
+- Hold the existing Pin control for Super Pin. Move/resize the second panel and verify its position survives a later recreation/restart. Hold Dual View for Triple View: Detach moves the complete combined view, preserving the split. Its secondary toolbar's Detach controls the combined host. Super Pin retains independent geometry.
+- Exercise page-push, pin, expand/restore and hover hide/reveal in both docked and detached modes. Page-push remains the existing user choice; detaching does not silently toggle it.
+- Use a slow page to test Reload/Stop on both primary and secondary toolbars. A main tab's loading state must not affect either control.
+- Save the current page as the app start URL. A normal primary app updates its URL; Essential/tab-linked and secondary actions create a new standalone app. They do not alter the source tab's URL or identity. The app limit still applies.
+- Toggle the Mobile pill button and verify container/site identity after the expected reload. Try a real-tab add-on host, including a site with forms.
+- Press Ctrl/Cmd+L with focus in each panel, then outside panels. Native browser URL-bar behavior should remain outside panel focus.
+- Select light/dark/system/content policies and high contrast. Check tooltip text, pill controls, custom themes and settings window readability.
+- Play a captioned video. Under Video playback, switch Subtitle placement between Below and Overlay; try size/line limits and disable captions. Verify the picture is not covered by the separate band and empty captions reserve no space. Existing source support and capture limitations still apply.
+
+## Companion mods
+
+The owner recommends **Tab Groups by oom333** and uses it with Zentral Groups disabled. The Zentral Groups settings remain for users who prefer them. Enable Compatibility → Use external Tab Groups to pause Zentral's group hooks without deleting state. Do not enable both group implementations intentionally unless testing their interaction.
+
+Compatibility → Use external Library layout pauses Extended's experimental Library geometry for users who want ZenLibraryTweaks/native Library layout to own it. Other existing integration switches (Arc styling, native hover, browser hosts and website styles) remain separate. No companion mod is installed, enabled or modified by this ZIP.
+
+## Broader regression pass
+
+Use left/right sidebar, collapsed/expanded/compact, vertical app bar and top-toolbar layouts; different window sizes and a second window; multiple workspaces; Apps disabled; module disable/re-enable; Sine hot unload; context-menu Copy/Open Link; pointer cancellation/window blur during a drag; background audio and badges; full/SPA navigation and process swaps. Test a fresh profile as well as your existing profile.
+
+Classic Extended geometry remains selectable. It restores the legacy shared-offset behavior; the hybrid's saved rectangles remain stored for switching back. Global legacy offset/docking settings establish initial/reset placement, while saved hybrid placements retain each app's chosen side and rectangle.
+
+## Automated verification and limits
+
+The build runs syntax/JSON/resource/schema checks, module declaration and loader tests, the actual adapted Apps bridge contract, pure geometry tests, DOM integration tests and caption layout tests. Mock DOM tests do not emulate Gecko, XUL remote frames, the compositor, Sine's registration cache, or companion mod execution. These live-browser checks are still required before treating 3.0.0 as validated for your configuration.
+
+If a problem occurs, record the exact Zen/Sine/OS versions, layout, involved app/panel type, whether Hybrid or Classic geometry is selected and the reproduction steps. Ctrl+Alt+= opens bootstrap diagnostics if startup fails. Include the diagnostic export, with private URLs removed if sharing it.
+
+Rollback: close Zen and restore the old folder. The new placement preferences are additive; the original app records, group data, old offsets, browser assignments and mobile-ID store remain in their existing format.
