+# Persistent panel placement and 1.1.0 controls
+
+Entrypoint: `ZentralPanelEnhancements.js`, catalog feature `panel-enhancements`. Requires the panel coordinator and base bridge. Styles and `settings.json` are owned here.
+
+Owns per-app placement, snap previews, temporary pinning, optional pill controls, start-URL actions, Reload/Stop UI and focus-scoped Ctrl/Cmd+L. Pure rectangle calculations live in `zentral/geometry/`. It reuses the panel coordinator's progress observations and existing browser/container identity functions; it does not move or recreate browsers for geometry.
+
+Placement is stored in `zen.workspace.zentral.hybrid.placements` as version 1. Keys distinguish primary versus secondary role, app identity, and optional workspace. The default scope is per app; global and per-workspace scopes are selectable. Writes merge the live pref and commit at gesture boundaries. Closing/reopening and browser restarts preserve position. A temporarily smaller viewport clamps the live rectangle without overwriting the desired stored rectangle.
+
+Hybrid geometry owns the entire primary root (including both Triple View slots) and the separate Super Pin shell. Classic Extended geometry remains selectable and uses the prior shared offsets. Legacy docking/offset settings establish initial/reset geometry; saved hybrid entries retain the user's per-app choice. Overflow is an explicit option, separate from hover hiding. Reset position is on tile and panel-chrome RMB menus.
+
+Detaching temporarily pins the primary. Clicking Pin while detached changes the state restored on docking; holding Pin still selects Super Pin. Detached surfaces expose eight resize directions. Docked all-sides controls still follow the existing preference. Moving the anchored edge away from its dock detaches it; moving near an edge shows a cancellable snap preview.
+
+Resource ownership: Core lifecycle owns listeners, coalesced UI frames, preference observers and timeouts; a gesture owns pointer capture, shield, ghost and drag state. Cancellation restores the starting placement/pin. No new permanent polling or independent progress-listener graph is installed.
+
+Normal app start-URL changes use B002. Essential/tab-linked and secondary actions create an independent app from the loaded URL. They do not move the tab or change its assigned container. Existing app limits and URL validation apply. Source files and `TESTING.md` describe the live Gecko verification still needed.
